1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,440
想象一下，只用一句话就能提出视频需求
Imagine asking for a video with one sentence:

2
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:08,912
用瑞士风格解释我的 Cursor 技能，五分钟，配中英双语字幕
explain my Cursor skills, in Swiss style, five minutes, with bilingual subtitles.

3
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:11,580
你不必每次都重新
You should not have to describe the fonts,

4
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:14,571
描述字体、节奏、结构和导出设置
pacing, structure, and export settings every time.

5
00:00:14,891 --> 00:00:20,459
可复用的技能会保存这些决定，让下一次请求专注于要讲的主题
A reusable skill stores those decisions, so your next request can focus on the topic.

6
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:26,385
技能就像食谱：它说明何时使用工作流、要按哪些步骤操作
A skill is a recipe: when to use a workflow, what steps to follow,

7
00:00:26,385 --> 00:00:28,398
以及合格的结果包含什么
and what a good result contains.

8
00:00:28,566 --> 00:00:32,683
工具是厨具，比如视频渲染器或图像生成器
Tools are equipment, such as a video renderer or image generator.

9
00:00:33,003 --> 00:00:35,755
Cursor、Codex 和 Claude Code 则是厨师
Cursor, Codex, and Claude Code are the cooks.

10
00:00:36,075 --> 00:00:40,577
共享食谱，并不会自动让每位厨师拥有相同的厨具
Sharing a recipe does not automatically give every cook the same equipment.

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,625
你的 Mac 已经有一个共享起点
Your Mac already has a shared starting point.

12
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:48,710
在安装这次的新技能之前，审计发现你的主目录下
Before this installation, the audit found eighty-three skill

13
00:00:48,710 --> 00:00:52,412
点 agents 里的 skills 文件夹中有八十三个技能文件夹
folders under dot agents, then skills, in your home folder.

14
00:00:52,567 --> 00:00:56,195
Cursor 还在点 cursor 里的 skills-cursor
Cursor separately maintained twenty-five skills under dot cursor,

15
00:00:56,195 --> 00:00:57,995
目录中单独维护了二十五个技能
then skills cursor.

16
00:00:58,071 --> 00:01:01,399
普通的点 cursor 下的 skills 文件夹当时并不存在
The ordinary dot cursor skills folder did not exist.

17
00:01:01,719 --> 00:01:05,516
相近的名称，可能代表不同的位置和管理者
Similar names can describe very different locations and owners.

18
00:01:07,333 --> 00:01:10,792
在点 cursor 中，extensions 提供编辑器功能
Inside dot cursor, extensions add editor features.

19
00:01:10,792 --> 00:01:15,288
plugins 打包助手能力，projects 保存工作状态
Plugins bundle agent capabilities. Projects stores working state,

20
00:01:15,288 --> 00:01:21,029
MCP 配置定义工具连接，而 hooks 可以触发命令
while the M C P configuration names tool connections and hooks can launch commands.

21
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,336
插件缓存可能保留同一技能的多个版本
Plugin caches can keep several versions of one skill.

22
00:01:24,656 --> 00:01:27,835
文件存在，不代表应用正在加载它
A file's presence does not prove the application loads it.

23
00:01:28,155 --> 00:01:31,632
配套目录记录了所有观察到的副本
The companion catalog records all observed copies.

24
00:01:33,467 --> 00:01:36,842
在技能文件夹中，先找 SKILL.md
Inside a skill folder, find the skill markdown file.

25
00:01:36,842 --> 00:01:42,555
文件中的名称和描述说明何时使用它，正文则提供操作流程
Its name and description identify when it applies. The main text supplies the procedure.

26
00:01:42,734 --> 00:01:44,689
references 保存风格指南
References hold style guidance,

27
00:01:44,689 --> 00:01:48,601
scripts 自动完成渲染步骤，assets 提供模板
scripts automate rendering steps, and assets supply templates.

28
00:01:48,921 --> 00:01:53,230
它们一起把反复进行的对话变成可复用的包
Together they turn a repeated conversation into a reusable package.

29
00:01:53,550 --> 00:01:56,942
但这些指令仍然需要相应工具才能执行
Instructions still need tools capable of carrying them out.

30
00:01:58,767 --> 00:02:03,283
追溯来源时，要区分内容作者、管理文件的软件
To trace origin, distinguish the author, the software managing the files,

31
00:02:03,283 --> 00:02:05,083
以及执行安装的人或程序
and whoever installed them.

32
00:02:05,134 --> 00:02:08,586
例如，你的二十六份共享技能文件
For example, twenty-six shared skill files exactly

33
00:02:08,586 --> 00:02:12,935
与 Google Cloud Data Agent Kit
match copies inside your Google Cloud Data Agent Kit extension.

34
00:02:12,935 --> 00:02:17,353
扩展中的副本完全一致。 这证明内容相同，却不能证明是谁复制的
That proves matching content. It does not prove who copied them.

35
00:02:17,353 --> 00:02:23,843
清单和安装代码可以提供证据；仅凭时间戳无法确定安装者
Manifests and installer code provide evidence; timestamps alone cannot identify the installer.

36
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,768
是否有用，取决于具体任务
Usefulness depends on the job.

37
00:02:27,768 --> 00:02:31,972
Bedrock 和存储技能能帮助你处理 AWS 项目
Bedrock and storage skills can help with your A W S projects.

38
00:02:31,972 --> 00:02:36,452
Python 依赖和 notebook 技能则支持研究工作流
Python dependency and notebook skills support research workflows.

39
00:02:36,600 --> 00:02:42,498
制作视频时，优先考虑依据、讲解、视觉设计、旁白和渲染
For videos, prioritize evidence, explanations, visual design, narration, and rendering.

40
00:02:42,498 --> 00:02:48,802
专业技能留给相关主题使用
Keep specialist skills for relevant topics. A large collection is not automatically wasteful.

41
00:02:48,802 --> 00:02:53,005
技能多不等于浪费，装有指令也不代表连接的服务一定可用
Installed instructions do not prove a connected service works.

42
00:02:54,933 --> 00:02:57,745
新的技能库只保留一个可编辑来源
For the new library, keep one editable source

43
00:02:57,745 --> 00:03:01,056
放在主目录的点 agents 下的 skills 中
under your home folder's dot agents skills directory.

44
00:03:01,376 --> 00:03:06,240
当前的 Cursor 和 Codex 文档都支持这个位置
Current Cursor and Codex documentation both recognize this location.

45
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:12,098
Claude Code 则通过自己 skills 文件夹中的符号链接访问同一套文件
Claude Code gets a symbolic link from its own skills folder, pointing to the same files.

46
00:03:12,098 --> 00:03:13,598
因此修改来源一次即可
Edit the source once.

47
00:03:13,598 --> 00:03:17,493
由应用管理的技能和插件缓存仍保留在原位
Keep application-managed skills and plugin caches in place.

48
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:22,998
安装后，检查每个应用的技能选择器
After installation, check each application's skill picker.

49
00:03:22,998 --> 00:03:27,206
选中 Conny Explainer Video，先让它生成制作简报
Select Conny Explainer Video and first ask for a production brief.

50
00:03:27,206 --> 00:03:30,649
确认它采用了预期的风格预设和默认设置
Confirm that it uses the intended preset and defaults.

51
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,597
接着测试参数覆盖和短片渲染：应用能否找到技能、遵循指令，并产出结果？
Then test an override and a short render. Can the app find the skill, follow its instructions,

52
00:03:36,597 --> 00:03:40,421
远程电脑需要单独配置
and produce the result? Remote computers need their own setup.

53
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:45,764
预设菜单把你的偏好变成简短名称
The preset menu gives your preferences short names:

54
00:03:45,764 --> 00:03:50,377
瑞士风格、盒式未来主义、风格派、包豪斯、NASA 朋克、莱茵生命
Swiss, cassette futurism, De Stijl, Bauhaus, NASA punk, Rhine Lab,

55
00:03:50,377 --> 00:03:51,683
以及像素工作室
and pixel studio.

56
00:03:51,733 --> 00:03:56,512
你的科幻参考包括《星空》、NASA 朋克和莱茵生命
Your science-fiction references include Starfield, NASA punk, and Rhine Lab.

57
00:03:56,832 --> 00:04:01,525
每个预设都应定义配色、字体、构图和运动方式
Each preset should specify palette, typography, composition, and motion.

58
00:04:01,845 --> 00:04:06,560
风格名称会选中设计规范，实际样片才能展示效果
A style name selects a design brief; the rendered sample shows how well it works.

59
00:04:08,400 --> 00:04:13,713
这个工作流的默认简报是
For this workflow, the default brief is Swiss design, five minutes, ten eighty p,

60
00:04:13,713 --> 00:04:18,960
瑞士风格、五分钟、1080p、每秒三十帧、英语旁白，以及中英双语字幕
thirty frames per second, English narration, and Chinese plus English subtitles.

61
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:21,074
你只需说明要改的地方
You only need to state changes.

62
00:04:21,394 --> 00:04:24,082
要求两分钟，就会覆盖默认时长
Asking for two minutes overrides the duration.

63
00:04:24,402 --> 00:04:27,627
保存的工作流延续你惯用的选择
The saved workflow should carry your usual choices forward

64
00:04:27,627 --> 00:04:30,184
同时以你本次的要求为准
while keeping your current request in control.

65
00:04:31,967 --> 00:04:37,140
下次制作时，你可以说：使用 Conny Explainer Video
For your next video, say: use Conny Explainer Video to explain my Cursor skills,

66
00:04:37,140 --> 00:04:40,180
用瑞士风格解释我的 Cursor 技能，五分钟，中英双语字幕
Swiss style, five minutes, bilingual subtitles.

67
00:04:40,334 --> 00:04:42,496
我们的工作流分成三个角色
Our workflow separates three roles.

68
00:04:42,496 --> 00:04:48,426
导演核实事实并安排讲解顺序，设计师把这些想法变成画面
The director checks the facts and teaching sequence. The designer turns those ideas into frames.

69
00:04:48,426 --> 00:04:52,750
工程实现则负责时间安排、旁白、字幕和最终渲染
The engineer builds timing, narration, captions, and the final render.

70
00:04:52,900 --> 00:04:58,511
检查样片，调整保存的偏好，下次就能复用这份改进后的食谱
Review a sample, adjust the saved preferences, and reuse the improved recipe next time.
